1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,700
 If I woke up 30 pounds overweight tomorrow and want to lose it all by summer, here's exactly what I'd do.

2
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:07,640
 I'd follow the 12-10-8-4-1 fat loss method.

3
00:00:07,740 --> 00:00:11,160
 12 is for your calories. Take your current body weight and multiply it by the number 12.

4
00:00:11,280 --> 00:00:14,180
 So if you're 200 pounds, you'll be eating 2,400 calories daily.

5
00:00:14,280 --> 00:00:17,060
 This will create the caloric deficit required for you to lose weight.

6
00:00:17,220 --> 00:00:22,580
 10 is for your steps. You're going to get 10,000 steps daily to increase your activity levels and accelerate your fat loss.

7
00:00:22,820 --> 00:00:28,480
 8 is for your sleep. You're going to get 8 hours of sleep per night as this will help your body recover and make it easier for you to lose weight.

8
00:00:28,480 --> 00:00:31,320
 4 is for your workouts. You're going to lift weights 4 days per week.

9
00:00:31,420 --> 00:00:35,220
 This is going to burn calories, but it will also help you build muscle, which will increase your metabolism.

10
00:00:35,600 --> 00:00:39,760
 And 1 is for your protein. You're going to eat 1 gram of protein per pound of body weight.

11
00:00:39,860 --> 00:00:43,280
 This will help curb hunger cravings and make it easier for you to be in a caloric deficit.

12
00:00:43,480 --> 00:00:47,080
 And if you want my full fat loss meal guide, comment lean and I'll send it your way for free.

